{
    "_comment": "Awkward content for developers and CI: the cases that make a page break, not the clean content a user is shown (that is demo data, a different thing). Rows are written with the seed marker as an alias prefix, so `remove` finds exactly them. Keys are local to this file; studies name their teachers and series by key. `media` defaults to one YouTube link; each entry names a seeded server by addon type (the `servers` layer must have run) and must be a real public URL, because an invented path renders a broken player. `guest` is the HTTP status a logged-out visitor gets for the study's sermon page, checked by build/verify-frontend.php; it defaults to 200. `registered`, `editor` and `manager` are the same for a visitor logged in as that seeded account (the accounts layer), and default to 200 too. Observed and intended: a Registered member opens Registered-level studies but not Special-level or unpublished ones; editors and managers open everything. 404 for access-restricted content is the current behaviour, not necessarily the intended one: it is recorded here so a change to it is noticed.",
